kind is one of: workitem, page, project. project_id chooses the scope a write lands in; omit it for the workspace, which is also the only scope a project kind can live at. For a workitem or page kind, listing without project_id is the wider view: it returns a project's templates as well as the workspace's own, told apart by a non-null project. Pass project_id to list one project's alone. template_data is a JSON object holding what gets templated -- for a work item template, the fields a work item created from it starts with, such as {"name": "Spec", "description_html": "<p>Context / Acceptance criteria</p>", "priority": "medium"}. update merges it into what is there rather than replacing it, so pass only what changes. description is the template's own summary, not the templated body.

